WEBVTT

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.280
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.610
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.320
but also in crime.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.570
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.990
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.160
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:49.480
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:54.030
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.990 --> 00:01:01.580
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.000
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.250
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:19.970
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.100
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.100
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:33.190
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.200
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.620
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:48.040
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.380
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.550
You thief!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.150
What's going on here?

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.070
Kubo, did you start this?

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:23.450
That little pervert stole
all the fish I was drying!

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.370
How dare you insult
my precious Kumiko!

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.870
Shut up!

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.960
So what's the damage?

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.210
Let's see, three full
layers... that's 240 fish.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.880
240?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:44.310
Nice story, but no cat
on Earth can eat 240 fish!

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.100
Maybe it dug a
hole and hid them!

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.560
You're thinking of a dog.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.690
Anyway, she's sick
of your stinking fish!

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.860
It isn't even fit for seagulls!

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:54.860
Why you!

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.570
Is this what started the fight?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.990
Good specimen.
Very well preserved.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.160
This batch was perfect!

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.830
Decent aroma.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:11.080
You like it? I marinade it for
six hours before smoking it.

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:13.630
You're a true connoisseur!

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:17.920
I knew you'd appreciate
true art! Men like us...

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.920
You idiot!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.220
We don't have time for this!
Are you cooks or mechanics?

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:29.890
And Kazu - who told you it
was okay to bring in a feral cat?

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:30.890
Er... um...

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.610
If you're busy with cooking and
pets, you don't need time to fish!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.400
You won't be needing
the speedboat!

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.780
Fishing is forbidden
until further notice!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.360
But, Sir!

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.950
If I say it's forbidden, it's forbidden!
Shige, finish up here.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.370
In light of what
just happened...

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:57.040
Kubo and Ito are assigned
two weeks of bathroom duty.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.670
Now get back to work!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:02.680
The Underground Mystery Tour

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:09.430
So, have you noticed something
odd around here recently?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.470
Whaddya mean?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:15.100
I'm not sure, but it seems like a lot
of things have gone missing lately.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.190
Maybe I'm just being forgetful.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.190
Didn't we get cream?

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.570
I bought some yesterday.
Isn't it on the shelf?

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.200
Wasn't someone complaining
about losing his pickled meat?

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:32.790
The Captain lost some whiskey
out of his locked liquor cabinet.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:35.670
The good stuff he got
three years ago in Hachioji?

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:38.880
I didn't want to say anything...

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.210
but since we don't
get many visitors...

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.340
it must be someone here.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.380
You lost something?

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:49.890
Just some rice crackers
and chocolate. Not much.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.930
I thought Asuma had eaten it.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.020
Hey!

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.810
What's wrong, Hiromi?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.780
Kimie... Kimie and Miyoko!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:09.370
They were here last night.
I was just coming to feed them.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.530
Wild dogs?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.200
Ito's "little pervert?"

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.210
This is no longer funny.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.960
It doesn't look like anyone broke
in, and the cage is still secure.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.750
Hiromi!

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:26.260
Whether this is an insider or
someone from the outside...

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.930
this is definitely a crime.
We have to stop this.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.850
Starting tonight, we'll
mount an armed watch!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.600
I guess we'd better.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:40.650
We'd probably better
clear this with the Captain.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.360
Fine with me.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.840
Who's there?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:12.930
Attack, Wyndham!

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.580
That's strange.
I thought we had him cornered.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.720
Come out, villain!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.970
Shige, over here!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.060
Good boy!
Look, Shige!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.170
I never heard about any tunnel.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:35.760
I'm not surprised. It was used to
haul garbage out to the landfill.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.930
It was closed before
Special Vehicles moved in.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:43.600
Once the landfill was finished,
they no longer needed it...

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:50.490
but the tunnels still
crisscross this entire area.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.820
So how do you know this?

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.870
I heard people
talking, way back.

00:07:55.870 --> 00:08:02.290
Some workers died in the tunnel.
Their bodies were never found.

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.040
At least, that was the story.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:06.750
How gruesome.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.250
Hardly surprising.
These things happen.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:14.220
I'll bet they thought closing
the tunnel solved the problem.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:16.890
Can we seal it with concrete?

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:22.480
I know it's only food, and this
may be beyond our jurisdiction...

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.940
but this is a violation of police
property. We should solve this.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:29.900
Yeah, but...

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:38.280
So that's it. HQ won't give us
backup on such a trivial case...

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.200
but we ARE policemen.
We can handle this ourselves.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:48.670
Your job is to capture the
fugitive who's hiding down there.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:52.420
Thank you both for volunteering
for this difficult assignment.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:09:00.850
Captain Nagumo looks happy.
She got to dump it all on us.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.520
We're the only choice.
Division 1 is on standby.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.400
Close it up.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:06.080
Hey, Ota, isn't it kind
of creepy down here?

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:07.160
Show some backbone.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.330
This is Ota.
Commencing search. Over.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:14.300
This is HQ.
Activate your transponder. Over.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:21.430
It was short notice, but I was
able to dig up a really old map.

00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:23.930
Still, we're better off
with it than without it.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.640
Are Ota and Shinshi
going to be okay?

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.890
Why wouldn't they be?

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:45.700
Ota!

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.410
We're ready, Sir.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:38.460
It's been two hours since we
lost contact with Ota and Shinshi.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:43.680
We don't know what happened,
but since their radio is out...

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:47.010
we must presume
there is some difficulty.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.680
This may be a simple case, or...

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:50.390
A monster.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.900
Recovering Ota and
Shinshi is your top priority.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.190
Proceed with caution,
and stay in contact.

00:11:57.190 --> 00:12:01.190
Officer Kumagami and three
men, departing on the search.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.840
Good luck!
Try not to get killed! Take care!

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.630
Maybe we should've
just sealed it.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:27.300
There are things in this world
that it's best not to tamper with.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.640
Is it working?

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:36.060
This program's a last minute
rush job. A real clunker.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:36.940
Signal received.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.020
Good, pipe it through.

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.650
This is Hawkwind.
Do you read me?

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.990
Reading you loud and clear.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:49.240
We're 20 meters north,
now heading east.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:53.640
It's much larger
than I expected.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.690
Should we pull them out,
or send in reinforcements?

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.110
What's wrong?

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.230
They're picking up movement.
About 50 meters ahead of them.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.280
Asuma!

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:10.530
Something's moving.
It's coming this way!

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.930
What's wrong Shinohara?
Izumi?

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.290
Man, that surprised me!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.080
Ouch!

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:11.470
Noa, are you all right?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.100
I think so. Hiromi?

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:15.430
You're sitting on me.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:19.600
Miss Kumagami fainted,
but I think she's okay.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:24.940
I'm sure she's happier that way.
Noa, turn on your flashlight.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.360
I dropped it when we fell.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.530
Do you still have
your flare? Use that.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.320
Um...

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:01.430
Shinohara! Izumi!
Answer me! Kumagami, report!

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:04.480
We've lost their signal.
I don't know where they are.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:08.940
What now?
Send in another wave of kids?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:14.490
Too risky. We still don't
know what's down there.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:16.910
Contact HQ.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.500
What was that?

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:28.090
Maybe we should have sealed it?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.430
Time for an equipment check.
Noa, you go first.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:41.310
I have two shells for my M-31,
flares, and three caramels.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.980
I lost everything in
the panic back there.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.230
I have two shotguns
and three shells.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.110
I'm getting scared.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:54.110
And now for the
really bad news.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.030
What?

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:58.240
I lost the radio.
We can't contact the surface.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.330
Oh?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:06.210
That's not all.
I dropped the transponder, too.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.460
Then how are we
going to get back?

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.380
We're completely lost.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.760
What'll we do?

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.090
Got any ideas?

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.090
How should I know?

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.050
Then how do you
expect me to know?

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:22.020
So where are you leading us?

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.480
I was just wondering
that myself.

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:32.860
Hey...

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:34.190
What?

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.780
About those rats...

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.660
What about them?

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.740
Wasn't it kind of weird?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.290
Yeah, so?

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:45.540
They just ignored us.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.420
It was like something
was chasing them.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:53.300
Come on, what could possibly
chase a huge pack of rats?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:56.800
Well...

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:32.340
Shinshi!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.130
Asuma!

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:41.340
I was so scared!
It was horrible!

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:45.100
Okay, everything's all right now.
What happened?

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.560
An alligator!
A HUGE alligator!

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:52.330
Kimie!

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:58.050
How could they do this to you?

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.510
Where are we?

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:07.470
This is the Captain's whiskey!
Look, it says "Goto."

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:09.430
This is incredible!

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:13.020
This stuff looks
awfully familiar.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:16.610
We've found the
thief's hideout!

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.940
This guy is really riding
high on the hog!

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:25.910
After him!

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.160
Halt! Wait! Stop!

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:43.610
Fumihiro Tadayama, 42 years old.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:48.110
He was a temp worker at the
landfill, back in the fall of 1990.

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:52.240
After a spell of unemployment,
he returned to the landfill...

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.120
into the tunnels.

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:59.290
He's been stealing water and
power and living like a king.

00:21:59.790 --> 00:22:03.340
And they say there's nothing
but garbage in a landfill.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.380
But there's no food.

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:10.680
He stole a little at a time,
so we wouldn't get suspicious.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:16.180
The lonely emperor of a
secret underground kingdom.

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:18.810
Was he truly happy down there?

00:22:20.650 --> 00:22:22.270
Shinobu, are YOU happy?

00:22:22.900 --> 00:22:24.070
Seal it up.

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:29.860
We look after our own.

00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.240
We always return, even
from the depths of hell.

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:39.790
We return to ensure that no
man may ever repeat our errors.

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:06.030
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:08.110 --> 00:23:13.780
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:15.740
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:21.210
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:29.510
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:30.300 --> 00:23:31.760
I got it

00:23:31.970 --> 00:23:39.310
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:45.190
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:46.730
One more chance

00:23:46.940 --> 00:23:54.370
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:59.830
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:03.500
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:13.010
This story is fiction...

00:24:09.010 --> 00:24:13.010
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:19.560 --> 00:24:22.390
The A.V.S. 98 Mark 2?
What is that??

00:24:22.390 --> 00:24:25.900
Shinohara Industry's newest
labor, a mass market prototype!

00:24:25.900 --> 00:24:28.770
It's got great power and
maneuvering. It's awesome!

00:24:28.770 --> 00:24:30.530
So, it's different from
the last prototype?

00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:32.990
Yeah, my grandfather is marketing
it as the BEST labor ever!

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:35.200
I don't believe the hype.

00:24:35.200 --> 00:24:36.660
Then, why don't YOU try it out?

00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:40.910
Next Episode: Mass Market Product Plan!
Target, locked on!

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:45.120
Next episode

00:24:40.120 --> 00:24:45.120
Mass Market Product Plan!
